      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}=\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3})}{{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3)}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nApplying the root rule in the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}) & =\\sqrt[3]{10(3)-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{30-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3) & =(3)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3} & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
